{"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "wrap", "ucas": "wrap s", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "wrap", "exhaustive": true, "operations": [{"op": "2x", "type": "i8", "nuw": false, "unsigned_wrap_points": 128, "unsigned_wrap_example": "x=-128", "nsw": false, "signed_wrap_points": 128, "signed_wrap_example": "x=-128", "c_ub": true}, {"op": "2x + 1", "type": "i8", "nuw": true, "unsigned_wrap_points": 0, "nsw": true, "signed_wrap_points": 0, "c_ub": false}], "end_to_end": {"exact": false, "mismatch_points": 128, "mismatch_example": "x=-128", "exact_for": [[-64, 63]]}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "wrap analysis of s:\n  2x   (i8)\n      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128\n      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen\n  2x + 1   (i8)\n      nuw holds\n      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)\n  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128\n      exact for: -64..63\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}
